  "Question": "Margie bought \\(3\\) apples at a cost of \\(50\\) cents per apple. She paid with a \\(5\\)-dollar bill. How much change did Margie receive?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\$1.50\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\$2.00\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\$2.50\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\$3.00\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\$3.50\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Work in cents so that all amounts use the same unit. The three apples cost \\(3\\times50=150\\) cents. Margie's \\(5\\)-dollar bill is worth \\(500\\) cents, so her change is\n\\[\n500-150=350\\text{ cents}=\\$3.50.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\text{E}\\).",
